 "summaries": [
  {
   "section": "Tires",
   "text": "The tires are matched by brand. Both the rear tires and the front left tire show a minimum tread depth of 5/32\" and 6/32\", which indicates they will need replacement for preventive maintenance."
  },
  {
   "section": "Exterior",
   "text": "The exterior has minor scratches, which are typical for the mileage and are mostly too small to capture in photos. There is a mark on the rear bumper cover that does not appear to be caused by an impact. Additionally, four valve stem caps are needed. The window and door seals are intact. The panel gaps between the front and rear bumpers and the quarter panels are normal, as are the shut lines between the hood, doors, and surrounding panels. There are no dents, and the paint condition is good."
  },
  {
   "section": "Interior",
   "text": "There is light wear on the seats, which is typical for the mileage. The inner door panels show wear consistent with age and mileage. The interior trim also shows normal wear. I tested all seat features throughout the vehicle and did not identify any obvious faults. There were no indications of smoke or unusual odors. The climate control and radio/navigation systems appeared to function properly. All essential features, including windows, locks, mirrors, and gauges, were operating correctly. The sunroof glass opened and closed without issue."
  },
  {
   "section": "Mechanical",
   "text": "The exhaust shows some surface rust but has no leaks and sounds good. There were no key fobs provided with the vehicle. Brake and power steering fluid levels were appropriate, and the coolant had the correct color with no leaks in the system. There was no burning oil smell in the engine compartment after running the vehicle. Fasteners in the engine bay appeared intact, and hoses, belts, axle boots, and visible bushings appeared sound. No obvious leaks were noted from the engine or transmission."
  },
  {
   "section": "Road Test",
   "text": "I connected my scan tool to the vehicle's computer system and found a stored P0004 code, indicating that further diagnosis is needed. The vehicle started and idled normally, with no excessive smoke or steam emissions during warm-up. During the test drive, the ride, acceleration, and handling were normal. The engine was smooth and responsive."
  }
 ],
